## 🛡️ 5. Input Validation & Edge Case Testing (VT) - 20 Test Cases
*Protects the system against malicious entries, API abuse, and data corruption.*

### Boundary Input Rules
86. **VT-001**: Verify Donation listing blocks submission when preparation time is set to a future date.
87. **VT-002**: Verify Donation listing blocks submission when quantity is set to 0 or negative integers.
88. **VT-003**: Verify User Registration validates that password strength meets complexity guidelines (minimum 8 characters, numbers, and symbols).
89. **VT-004**: Verify geolocation inputs block latitude coordinates exceeding +/- 90 degrees.
90. **VT-005**: Verify geolocation inputs block longitude coordinates exceeding +/- 180 degrees.
91. **VT-006**: Verify NGO upload rejects non-PDF/non-image format files for licensing verification.
92. **VT-007**: Verify user fields reject names exceeding 100 characters to prevent buffer issues.

### API Abuse & Security Protection
93. **VT-008**: Verify JWT validator returns `403 Forbidden` if role fields do not match route constraints.
94. **VT-009**: Verify rate-limiting middleware (`apiLimiter`) rejects requests when client queries exceed 100 requests per 15 minutes.
95. **VT-010**: Verify database endpoints sanitize inputs to prevent NoSQL injection attempts.
96. **VT-011**: Verify HTML sanitizer strips script tags from chat message payloads before rendering to prevent XSS.
97. **VT-012**: Verify update user endpoints prevent modification of internal credentials (like roles and trust score values).
98. **VT-013**: Verify claiming endpoints block users from updating status fields of archived donations.

### Concurrent Operations & Fail-Safes
99. **VT-014**: Verify two NGOs attempting to claim the same donation concurrently result in one success and one rejection.
100. **VT-015**: Verify socket server blocks users from joining socket rooms they are not authorized participants of.
101. **VT-016**: Verify connection layer blocks double login triggers on separate tabs if session limits are enforced.
102. **VT-017**: Verify server returns clean error statuses rather than failing when database connection times out.
103. **VT-018**: Verify image upload limits block payloads larger than 10MB to maintain network performance.
104. **VT-019**: Verify recovery triggers send one email per password reset request to prevent spamming.
105. **VT-020**: Verify notification payloads fallback gracefully when the target device push tokens are expired.

